 Flux's conditioning as Forge's Flux engine builds it (diffusion_engine/
 flux.py get_learned_conditioning): crossattn is the T5 engine's output for
 the prompt, and vector is CLIP-L's pooled output of the prompt's first chunk,
 the final-normed hidden state at its first EOS with no projection, taken
 before emphasis. wl is loaded with clip-l-flux-spec from clip_l.safetensors
 under flux-clip-l-layout.

 We say:

Section: Conditioning

  FluxCond = record {
    fc-t5 : Integer,
    fc-rows : Integer,
    fc-pooled : Integer,
    fc-status : Integer
  }

 status 0, or -1 when T5 failed and the CLIP encoder's status otherwise.

  flux-condition : T5File, T5Tok, ClipWeights, ClipBpe, Text -> FluxCond
  flux-condition (tf) (tok) (wl) (bpe) (prompt) =
    let t = t5-condition tf tok prompt
    in let cs = clip-prompt-chunks bpe prompt
    in let ol = clip-encode wl ((list-at cs 0).cc-ids)
    in let f = ce-free-all [ol.co-cond] 0
    in let status = if t.t5k-h == 0 then 0 - 1 else ol.co-status
    in FluxCond { fc-t5 = t.t5k-h, fc-rows = t.t5k-chunks * t.t5k-rows, fc-pooled = ol.co-pooled, fc-status = status }

